 avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{10}) & ≈\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3.162\\,278) \\\\  & ≈1.151\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087683 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d82c39c-5ec6-5cf3-96f8-e778091a451a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions Containing Natural Logarithms Using a Calculator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1094c280-8d50-5ac3-af86-01d3f0f6eb50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.852" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522051} {:answer/id #uuid "32371844-26f7-59d5-a03a-49495028005e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.793" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522130} {:answer/id #uuid "de1a7a07-4e4a-5e7b-b5e1-fb4988240ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.802" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522484} {:answer/id #uuid "df418158-2acd-5aa2-8cab-77fcb44d6ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522489} {:answer/id #uuid "edb23120-fe41-58c2-9bdf-75c119e10310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.863" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df418158-2acd-5aa2-8cab-77fcb44d6ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522489} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f063cea-5b17-54cf-988c-eca299598b1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00510ebe-a387-562e-98da-516fa9a673e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-99695" :question/problem "Using suitable approximations, calculate $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$ to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "We compute the required expression to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & ≈\\sqrt{1.386\\,294}\\cdot 0.693\\,147 \\\\  & ≈1.177\\,410\\cdot 0.693\\,147 \\\\  & ≈0.816\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
